#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110213 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "91100afb-9a36-57c0-9f30-4692cfef0b93" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Secant-Tangent and Other Identities"}] :question/id #uuid "3d64bc1e-3937-5e0d-b0f8-7dd06acd27ef" :question/math-academy-id "e-10052" :question/problem "Express $2\\tan x\\cdot(\\cot x+\\tan{x})$ in terms of $\\sec x$ only." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+\\tan^2 x = \\sec^2{x}\n$$\n\nAlso, recall the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\cot x = \\dfrac{1}{\\tan x}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\tan x\\cdot \\cot x = 1\n$$\n\nUsing the above identities, we can simplify our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\tan x \\cdot (\\cot x + \\tan x) &= 2\\tan x \\cdot \\cot x + 2\\tan^{2} x \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot 1 + 2\\tan^{2} x \\\\\n&= 2(1 + \\tan^{2} x) \\\\\n&= 2\\sec^{2} x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n2\\tan x\\cdot(\\cot x+\\tan{x})= 2\\sec^2x\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110214 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7640012b-79f9-5f6b-a26b-a7f4fe8c0e7b" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Secant-Tangent Identity: Replacing a Squared Secant"}] :question/id #uuid "c04610a2-f73f-57a9-b17b-da9b30a5e431" :question/math-academy-id "e-10053" :question/problem "Express $(1-\\sec x)(1+\\sec x)$ in terms of $\\tan x$ only." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+\\tan^2 x = \\sec^2{x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we expand the parentheses using the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\n(1-\\sec x)(1+\\sec x) = 1 - \\sec^2x\n$$\n\nThen, we rewrite the expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n1 - \\sec^{2} x &= 1 - (1 + \\tan^{2} x) \\\\\n&= 1 - 1 - \\tan^{2} x \\\\\n&=-\\tan^{2} x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n(1-\\sec x)(1+\\sec x)= -\\tan^2 x\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110368 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "03491655-9b81-5fc0-bf20-e4f74a9c72ad" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Secant-Tangent Identity: Replacing a Squared Tangent"}] :question/id #uuid "b34736aa-e682-5ab3-85a0-dd86f49759f1" :question/math-academy-id "e-3143" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\dfrac{2\\sec^2 \\theta}{1+\\tan^2 \\theta}$." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+\\tan^2 \\theta = \\sec^2{\\theta}\n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2\\sec^2 \\theta}{\\color{blue}1+\\tan^2 \\theta} = \\dfrac{2\\sec^2 \\theta}{\\color{blue}\\sec^2 \\theta}\n$$\n\nWe now cancel the common factor of $\\sec^2 \\theta$ in the numerator and denominator and simplify the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{2\\sec^{2} θ}{\\sec^{2} θ} &= \\frac{2\\sec^{2} θ}{\\sec^{2} θ} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2 \\cdot 1}{1} \\\\\n&= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2\\sec^2 \\theta}{1+\\tan^2 \\theta} = 2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268166 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "91100afb-9a36-57c0-9f30-4692cfef0b93" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Secant-Tangent and Other Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eecb07f1-889b-5ba4-854b-e58648fb61df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cot}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268168} {:answer/id #uuid "6fa2ffd7-2ee8-5427-ac7b-b5b0d1e8b677" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268169} {:answer/id #uuid "9dbcbcee-46a6-5394-af9b-219426cb7ba0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{cot}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268170} {:answer/id #uuid "f87f82a8-a459-5a72-8d15-154d1a5275ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268171} {:answer/id #uuid "ab5dc266-2ff0-5156-9598-99fdcd9e2055" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eecb07f1-889b-5ba4-854b-e58648fb61df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cot}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268168} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0657fd9-1a57-5f31-bc7e-763f21efc77b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268167}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c8899a82-fde3-5944-a023-fb73a996cbeb" :question/math-academy-id "q-120631" :question/problem "$\\frac{1}{(1-{cos}^{2}⁡x)(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{(1-{cos}^{2}⁡x)(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)} & =\\frac{1}{(1-{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\cdot ({sec}^{2}⁡x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we recall the following identities:\n\n$$\n1-{cos}^{2}⁡x={sin}^{2}⁡x,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},\\,\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\n$$\n\n \n\nUsing the above identities, we can further simplify our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{(1-{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\cdot ({sec}^{2}⁡x)} & =\\frac{1}{({sin}^{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & ={cot}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{(1-{cos}^{2}⁡x)(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)}={cot}^{2}⁡x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268173 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "91100afb-9a36-57c0-9f30-4692cfef0b93" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Secant-Tangent and Other Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5849eeb1-819b-572c-8465-9a8e465d6a82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268175} {:answer/id #uuid "bac07f71-f9fb-56e9-87a8-d240cddcebca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268176} {:answer/id #uuid "1ac8e8a4-f860-53e7-b746-b824c366b4bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268177} {:answer/id #uuid "f263fee3-0f62-5f75-bb27-1be1cefd6482" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268178} {:answer/id #uuid "64db3bd8-6ac0-51e7-8316-c12987d0c3de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268179}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64db3bd8-6ac0-51e7-8316-c12987d0c3de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268179} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5eac0bc-9085-598b-a740-71487f19df58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268174}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6d679bb5-0690-5683-8f8d-96c23c27401a" :question/math-academy-id "q-120639" :question/problem "$\\frac{{sec}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sec}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{{sec}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta }\n$$\n\nWe now simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sec}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\cancel{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the following identities: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta },\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta },\n$$\n\n \n\nUsing the above identities, we can further simplify our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sec}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268180 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "91100afb-9a36-57c0-9f30-4692cfef0b93" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Secant-Tangent and Other Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d50eb8bd-ddbd-553f-ad34-fd6713a4412a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268182} {:answer/id #uuid "2bb8c104-6231-5b9a-b6dc-ad74a7ad86b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268183} {:answer/id #uuid "8df093f7-9d2b-55a3-81f5-6c3898f28d3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268184} {:answer/id #uuid "e9bb77dc-48c4-5d8d-a842-5b38abc68ef7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268185} {:answer/id #uuid "17bc3e17-e07d-51c4-8956-02dbcc3ddc10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268186}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8df093f7-9d2b-55a3-81f5-6c3898f28d3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268184} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1419d8f-0e0e-512d-b217-ef5f5049d44c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268181}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9b0ff6e0-8d93-5dab-8902-8d6dc2a4a232" :question/math-academy-id "q-120651" :question/problem "$\\frac{{sec}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sec}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{{sec}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta }\n$$\n\nWe now simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sec}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{sec}^{2}}\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\cancel{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\n$$\n\n \n\nUsing the above identity, we can further simplify our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }}\\cdot \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sec}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268187 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "03491655-9b81-5fc0-bf20-e4f74a9c72ad" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Secant-Tangent Identity: Replacing a Squared Tangent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f695013-a469-5d70-ad2d-30fccfaffc19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{3}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268189} {:answer/id #uuid "b95f272b-774f-57b1-8298-cd580024f157" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268190} {:answer/id #uuid "fda5bf54-f65c-5463-ae78-cfd5ad51a7f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{sec}^{3}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268191} {:answer/id #uuid "3d9e372d-8cf4-507e-8f9e-2cfd49c7a98f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268192} {:answer/id #uuid "8e3410d8-a7f4-5be0-8053-b29cdf793351" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f695013-a469-5d70-ad2d-30fccfaffc19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{3}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268189} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d9184d6-17e0-5805-9109-10c4ced18d8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268188}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4d79e56a-d16f-561e-a310-5e542606beb8" :question/math-academy-id "q-142764" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\text{ }\\theta =$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\text{ }\\theta  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\text{ }\\,({tan}^{2}⁡\\theta +1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\text{ }\\,({sec}^{2}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & ={sec}^{3}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\text{ }\\theta ={sec}^{3}⁡\\theta .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268194 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "03491655-9b81-5fc0-bf20-e4f74a9c72ad" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Secant-Tangent Identity: Replacing a Squared Tangent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7f7e5ad-a986-537a-bbb2-e380fc784515" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268196} {:answer/id #uuid "a590a3ca-5b68-5027-8fa1-18aee9106c28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{sec}^{2}+4\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268197} {:answer/id #uuid "89f9df74-1010-54e5-a707-a7da174b5337" :a